GM</given-names></name><name><surname>Sykora</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2004</year><article-title>Neuroleptic drug therapy in older adults newly admitted to nursing homes: incidence, dose, and specialist contact</article-title><source>J Am Geriatr Soc</source><volume>52</volume><fpage>749</fpage><lpage>55</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15086656</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b9-ndt-2-521"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Byerly</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Weber</surname><given-names>MT</given-names></name><name><surname>Brooks</surname><given-names>DL</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2001</year><article-title>Antipsychotic medications and the elderly: effects on cognition and implications for use</article-title><source>Drugs Aging</source><volume>18</volume><fpage>45</fpage><lpage>61</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11232738</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b10-ndt-2-521"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Caroff</surname><given-names>SN</given-names></name><name><surname>Mann</surname><given-names>SC</given-names></name><name><surname>Keck</surname><given-names>PE</given-names><suffix>Jr</suffix></name></person-group><year>1998</year><article-title>Specific treatment of the neuroleptic malignant syndrome</article-title><source>Biol Psychiatry</source><volume>44</volume><fpage>378</fpage><lpage>81</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9777166</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b11-ndt-2-521"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cohen-Mansfield</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><year>1986</year><article-title>Agitated behaviors in the elderly. II. Preliminary results in the cognitively deteriorated</article-title><source>J Am Geriatr Soc</source><volume>34</volume><fpage>722</fpage><lpage>7</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3760436</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b12-ndt-2-521"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cohen-Mansfield</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Werner</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Marx</surname><given-names>MS</given-names></name></person-group><year>1989</year><article-title>An observational study of agitation in agitated nursing home residents</article-title><source>Int Psychogeriatr</source><volume>1</volume><fpage>153</fpage><lpage>65</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2491142</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b13-ndt-2-521"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cole</surname><given-names>SA</given-names></name><name><surname>Saleem</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Shea</surname><given-names>WP</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>Ziprasidone for agitation or psychosis in dementia: four cases</article-title><source>Int J Psychiatry Med</source><volume>35</volume><fpage>91</fpage><lpage>8</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15977947</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b14-ndt-2-521"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>Committee on Safety of Medicines/Medicines Control Agency</collab></person-group><year>2001</year><article-title>QT interval prolongation with antipsychotics</article-title><fpage>27</fpage><fpage>4</fpage></citation></ref><ref id="b15-ndt-2-521"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cummings</surname><given-names>JL</given-names></name><name><surname>Mega</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Gray</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>1994</year><article-title>The Neuropsychiatric Inventory: comprehensive assessment of psychopathology in dementia</article-title><source>Neurology</source><volume>44</volume><fpage>2308</fpage><lpage>14</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7991117</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b16-ndt-2-521"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Davidson</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Harvey</surname><given-names>PD</given-names></name><name><surname>Vervarcke</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2000</year><article-title>A long-term, multicenter, open-label study of risperidone in elderly patients with psychosis. On behalf of the Risperidone Working Group</article-title><source>Int J Geriatr Psychiatry</source><volume>15</volume><fpage>506</fpage><lpage>14</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10861916</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b17-ndt-2-521"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>De Deyn</surname><given-names>PP</given-names></name><name><surname>Carrasco</surname><given-names>MM</given-names></name><name><surname>Deberdt</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2004</year><article-title>Olanzapine versus placebo in the treatment of psychosis with or without associated behavioral disturbances in patients with Alzheimer&#x02019;s disease</article-title><source>Int J Geriatr Psychiatry</source><volume>2</volume><fpage>115</fpage><lpage>26</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14758577</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b18-ndt-2-521"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>De Deyn</surname><given-names>PP</given-names></name><name><surname>Rabheru</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Rasmussen</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>1999</year><article-title>A randomized trial of risperidone, placebo, and haloperidol for behavioral symptoms of dementia</article-title><source>Neurology</source><volume